            <div xml:id="d331">

                <pb facs="0462" n="368" xml:id="pg368"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/859: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Reber</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-11-13T13:00:00-05:00">November 13, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>100. Your 155, November 12, noon. Your proposed action is approved. President
                    King’s reply and attitude in this connection should be immediately reported.</p>
                <p>The Liberian Consul General at Baltimore will be summoned on November 17 to the
                    Department to be questioned by me respecting these reports. This is for your
                    information and is not to be imparted to President King.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
